course: dictionary
lesson: 14176
title: Momentarily: a moment or very soon
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Momentarily» is a small word with a short time inside it. Its root is moment, so it usually means for a very short time, only a second or two. «She was momentarily blinded by the flash.» The flash was bright for a second, so her sight stopped for only a little while.
explain: Read the words around it to find its meaning. «The bus stopped momentarily at the traffic lights.» The lights are red for a moment, and then the bus goes on. Ask yourself: does the sentence tell me it was short, or that it will happen soon?
explain: In American English, «momentarily» can also mean very soon. «We will be landing momentarily» is an announcement on a plane. The pilot does not mean a second ago, but in a very short time. The words «will be» show that it is still to come.
fact: «Momentarily» means for a very short time, only a moment.
fact: «Momentarily» is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Momentarily blinded» means blinded for only a second or two.
fact: In American English, «momentarily» can mean very soon: «We will be landing momentarily.»
fact: Check the clues: if the sentence says «then» or «again», the event was probably short.
exercise: «The lights went out, and Sam was momentarily confused.» What does momentarily mean here? | For the whole day | Forever and ever | Very loudly | *For a very short time
exercise: A pilot says, «We will be landing momentarily.» What does momentarily mean? | Never | *Very soon | Yesterday | Very slowly
exercise: «The door opened momentarily, then shut again.» Which words show that it was only a short time? | opened | *then shut again | the door | blue
test: «The screen flickered momentarily before it went black.» What does momentarily mean? | For a long time | Very angrily | Never | *For a very short time
test: A teacher says, «The show starts momentarily.» What does momentarily mean? | Long ago | *Very soon | Not at all | Only once a year
exam: «She paused momentarily, then carried on walking.» What does momentarily mean? | *For only a moment | In a big, loud way | Very quietly and slowly | For the rest of the day
